---
/**
 * Problem framing — three vignettes of the audit gap.
 * Each maps to one ASD primitive: ledger / effects / audit stream.
 *
 *   Why?        → context rot in commit messages and .md files → Ledger
 *   What?       → side effects invisible until something breaks → Effects
 *   Who/when?   → no enforcement, no trail at scale → Audit stream
 */
---

<section class="section problem">
	<div class="container">
		<div class="eyebrow">
			<span class="dot"></span>
			<span class="eyebrow-text">THE_AUDIT_GAP.md</span>
		</div>
		<h2 class="section-title">Three flavors of the audit gap.</h2>
		<p class="section-lede">
			Every team using AI coding tools hits all three, even before they've
			named them. ASD's three primitives map one-to-one to the three
			versions of the problem.
		</p>

		<div class="vignettes">
			<article class="vignette v-why">
				<div class="v-label">01 // LEDGER</div>
				<h3>Nobody knows why it's written that way.</h3>
				<p class="scene">
					The agent used a mutex. Four months later a reviewer asks why.
					The commit message says "fix concurrency issue." There's no
					incident link, no invariant declared, no design decision on
					record. The code works but the reasoning is gone — and every
					future agent touching this file will re-derive or ignore it.
				</p>
				<p class="fix">
					<strong>ASD records why.</strong> A decision ledger keyed to
					symbols — not to files or commits. Append a hazard, a
					constraint, a rationale. It survives renames, supersedes stale
					entries, and surfaces in every MCP query about that symbol.
				</p>
			</article>

			<article class="vignette v-what">
				<div class="v-label">02 // EFFECTS</div>
				<h3>Nobody knows what it actually touches.</h3>
				<p class="scene">
					You refactored a helper. The agent said it was "pure." Two
					deploys later it's writing to disk in a path nobody anticipated.
					The declared effects said nothing. The transitive call graph
					wasn't checked. The blast radius was invisible until production.
				</p>
				<p class="fix">
					<strong>ASD tracks effects.</strong> 17 effect categories —
					io.fs, io.net, io.db, proc.spawn, env.read and more — declared
					per symbol and propagated transitively through the call graph.
					Run the tracer and observed effects confirm or contradict
					declared ones.
				</p>
			</article>

			<article class="vignette v-who">
				<div class="v-label">03 // AUDIT STREAM</div>
				<h3>Nobody can prove the process was followed.</h3>
				<p class="scene">
					Policy says hazard-class changes require human attestation.
					The agent appended a hazard note and deployed. Was there a
					review? The policy file existed but nothing enforced it on
					write. The audit trail is a git log — which doesn't distinguish
					agent commits from human commits, or approved changes from
					unchecked ones.
				</p>
				<p class="fix">
					<strong>ASD enforces and records.</strong> A file-backed policy
					gate intercepts every ledger write and effect declaration.
					Every decision — allow, deny, require-approval — emits a
					structured JSONL event. Every approval and rejection is recorded.
					One command verifies the chain was never tampered with.
				</p>
			</article>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<style>
	.problem {
		padding: 5rem 0;
	}

	.eyebrow {
		display: inline-flex;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 0.5rem;
		margin-bottom: 1rem;
	}

	.dot {
		width: 7px;
		height: 7px;
		border-radius: 50%;
		background: var(--asd-accent);
	}

	.eyebrow-text {
		font-family: var(--asd-font-mono);
		font-size: 0.7rem;
		letter-spacing: 0.1em;
		color: var(--asd-accent-text);
		text-transform: uppercase;
	}

	.vignettes {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
		gap: 1.5rem;
		margin-top: 2rem;
	}

	.vignette {
		background: var(--asd-panel);
		border: 1px solid var(--asd-border);
		border-radius: var(--asd-radius-lg);
		padding: 1.75rem;
	}

	.v-label {
		font-family: var(--asd-font-mono);
		font-size: 0.65rem;
		letter-spacing: 0.12em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
		font-weight: 700;
	}

	.v-why .v-label { color: var(--asd-accent); }
	.v-what .v-label { color: var(--asd-success); }
	.v-who .v-label { color: var(--asd-warn); }

	.v-why { border-top: 2px solid var(--asd-accent); }
	.v-what { border-top: 2px solid var(--asd-success); }
	.v-who { border-top: 2px solid var(--asd-warn); }

	h3 {
		font-size: 1.1rem;
		font-weight: 700;
		color: #ffffff;
		margin: 0 0 0.75rem 0;
		line-height: 1.3;
	}

	.scene {
		font-size: 0.875rem;
		color: var(--asd-text-dim);
		line-height: 1.65;
		margin: 0 0 1rem 0;
		padding-bottom: 1rem;
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--asd-border);
	}

	.fix {
		font-size: 0.875rem;
		color: var(--asd-text);
		line-height: 1.65;
		margin: 0;
	}

	.fix strong {
		color: #ffffff;
	}

	@media (max-width: 860px) {
		.vignettes {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
		}
	}
</style>
